/* Learning Data: Governance principles. The words of the series' labs (Take it apart) and scenarios (Make the call), in English, for
   the prologue (film 0) and its ten films. Keep the keys in step with learn.es.js. One playground for each film, each on the chapter it
   plays (film, chapter), with three to five experiments (w.goals) the visitor ticks by making them happen; and twelve situations, the
   series' evaluation, each pointing to its playground. learn.js draws every picture from these words and keeps progress in this
   browser under "ld-data-governance": the labs visited, the experiments ticked, and the answers by scenario number (film × 10 + its
   place; the prologue's are 1 to 9).
   A page shows each situation's options in the order written here: the right answers are spread across the places, and the
   Spanish pack keeps them in the same places.
   build_series.py (series_learn) reads the first keys of each lab, in this order: id, kind, film, chapter, c, name; and of each
   scenario: type, n, lab, film. No other object here starts with id, and no other key is called kind or starts an object with type.
   The series' first part: papers and people, never code, file paths or tool screens. Names, numbers and dates follow each film's
   narration: Yusuf Demir, Mei, Jun, Sam, Clara in Planning, Tom's learning team, Marta's wallet team, Anil in the Faculty of Health,
   4,812 and 4,867, the binder's 215 lines. The bank in the prologue's playground and its figures are invented, for comparing choices. */
